<<EasyHelp_Options.txt>>
test2
test3
execase 1
show The Course 1 Minute is set to start within a minute, and run for one minute. Its time to Course closure (Disqualification) is set to one minute also.
show The course 5 Minutes starts in about 3 minutes, has a duration to Finish time of five minutes, and a further time to disqualification of three minutes.
show
show You will see that the Course Start time box flashes yellow for fifteen minutes before a Course Start Time. 
show This warns you to give Briefing instructions, and ensure that each Tag has been punched by a BRIEF Punch.
show 
show When any Course starts, both its Start and Finish time boxes are coloured green.
show After a Course Finish Time, the Finish Time box is coloured Red. It remains coloured until the Disqualification Time.
show 
show When you have read this, you can continue the Tutorial anytime by reading the spare Tag you have.
show The Tutorial will step automatically through, each time you read the Tag again.
execase 2
tag1 ARAO
show Team 73 first Tag. Note the Progress Bar at the bottom of the window shows half-way.
show
show Note that the COURSE box saying Course 15 in 23 is yellow, as long as the Tag is connected.
show
show Also note that the first two Punches have been dis-allowed because no BRIEF punch was used.
show 
show You can correct this later.
show 
show     Read your TAG again to continue.
tag2 AKAG
show Team 73 second Tag. Note progress bar full. You should get a team printout.
show 
show     Read your TAG again to continue.
tag3 AFAH
show Team 38 first Tag. Notice that the Course label Course 6Hr has a yellow background before the Tag is removed.
show 
show Also note that Punch 40 is part of a Group of Punches and has been replaced by the Group Master punch, 46
show 
show     Read your TAG again to continue.
tag4 AEAO
show Second Tag for team 38. Expect a printout.
show 
show     Read your TAG again to continue.
tag5 AAAM
show Team 7 first Tag.
show 
show     Read your TAG again to continue.
tag6 AXAF
show Team 7 second tag. Expect a team Printout.
show 
show     Read your TAG again to continue.
tag7 ARAT
show   Team 137 has not been given a Course, so it scores in the default Course 0.
show 
show     Keep reading a TAG to continue scoring the event.
tag8 ASAT
show Team 137 printout. Ignore the fact that the Progress Bar is not full.
show 
show     Keep reading a TAG to continue scoring the event.
tag9 AFAG
show   Read the next Tag
tag10 ADAQ
show   Team 37 printout
tag11 AEAN
show   Read the next Tag
tag12 ADAO
show   Get a printout for Team 35

show 
show 
show Next, you will try re-scoring Team 35 to allow the Punch 43 used after the Start, but cancelled because no BRIEF Punch had been used.
show 
show    Remove the Tag, then
show    Click NEXT to continue
execase 5
test 
show Click the yellow HERE for COMPLAINTS Button.
show 
show Ignore a warning message about not all Tags scored.
show 
show Then click   BRIEF Punch in the white box which appears.
show 
show Now, you must re-insert the Tag which needs correcting, to select the correct scored record.
show 
show In this Tutorial, use the Tag you have been using all along.
show 
show When you remove the Tag, the Window which allows changing the BRIEF line appears.
execase 2
tag9 AFAG
show Remove the Tag
show 
show When removed, click the Brief from Line 1 button, or use the scroll buttons beside it to select the Brief line you want to allow.
show In this case, it will be Line 1.
show Note that although the 30 points for punch 32 are shown, the final score has not altered because the other Tag in the team has not scored Punch 32.
show 
show When the score window looks correct, click the SAVE Button to register the change.
show Click NEXT when you have allowed a Manual BRIEF and SAVED it.
execase 5
test
show  Now read the other Tag for team 35, because it needs changing too. 
show Just use the same Tag as before, in the Tutorial. 
show 
show   Read it now.
tag10 ADAQ
show Accept the BRIEF from line 1 as before, click SAVE as before, and now click PRINT.
show 
show 
show When finished, click the yellow Button "Click HERE to Resume NORMAL scoring."
show 
show Then you can resume scoring as usual,by reading the next Tag.
